1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:22,900
Good morning.

2
00:00:22,900 --> 00:00:26,100
How's everybody doing this morning?

3
00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:27,780
You don't have to say good.

4
00:00:27,780 --> 00:00:29,100
Remember, we just talked about it.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:30,840
You don't have to say good.

6
00:00:30,840 --> 00:00:32,120
I know, that's the temptation.

7
00:00:32,120 --> 00:00:34,240
We've got to say good when the pastor asks how we're doing.

8
00:00:34,240 --> 00:00:39,100
Hey, I want to just be over clear, over the top.

9
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:43,760
The youth meeting at the Miller's house, not my house.

10
00:00:43,760 --> 00:00:46,580
The other Miller's house, all right?

11
00:00:46,580 --> 00:00:52,560
It's not that I'm opposed to youth hanging out at my house, but it is Master's Weekend,

12
00:00:52,560 --> 00:00:55,020
and at the Miller house, that is a religious holiday.

13
00:00:55,020 --> 00:00:59,880
The fact that I'm here is a miracle this morning, okay?

14
00:01:00,660 --> 00:01:02,600
So, enjoy the Miller's house.

15
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:05,300
You can come to my house another time, but it's not going to be this weekend, okay?

16
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:07,160
I just want to make sure nobody shows up to my house.

17
00:01:07,160 --> 00:01:09,700
All right, I had to get that off my chest.

18
00:01:09,700 --> 00:01:10,820
Let's pray one more time.

19
00:01:12,580 --> 00:01:15,320
Father, Father, you are so, so good.

20
00:01:15,320 --> 00:01:22,100
And yet, often in our experiences, God, we feel your absence.

21
00:01:22,100 --> 00:01:26,120
We get frustrated with the circumstances of our life.

22
00:01:26,120 --> 00:01:27,360
We believe that you're good.

23
00:01:27,360 --> 00:01:30,660
We know it in our minds, but we don't always feel it in our bones.

24
00:01:30,660 --> 00:01:34,380
God, sometimes we need the Scriptures.

25
00:01:34,380 --> 00:01:35,440
We need songs.

26
00:01:35,600 --> 00:01:39,160
We need brothers and sisters to come around us and just to remind us that you're good.

27
00:01:39,160 --> 00:01:44,860
And so this morning, God, I pray this morning would be a reminder that you're good.

28
00:01:44,860 --> 00:01:49,380
That we believe it in our bones, not just in our minds.

29
00:01:50,480 --> 00:02:01,200
And that we would angle our lives in the direction that confirms and reminds us of your goodness.

30
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:03,740
It's in Jesus' name I pray.

31
00:02:03,740 --> 00:02:04,480
Amen.

32
00:02:04,480 --> 00:02:09,500
If you could throw the quadrant up for me real quick, I just want to let people know where we're at this morning.

33
00:02:10,420 --> 00:02:16,220
Last week, Matt talked about kind of, he gave the overview of the whole thing, and he talked about wonder and delight.

34
00:02:16,220 --> 00:02:17,040
Right?

35
00:02:17,040 --> 00:02:20,560
And this is often the experience that we have when we first come to know Jesus.

36
00:02:20,560 --> 00:02:30,420
Like, we had this revelation that we were sinners separated from God, that our life trajectory wasn't leading us anywhere good.

37
00:02:30,420 --> 00:02:34,160
We surrender our life to Jesus, and things get better.

38
00:02:34,160 --> 00:02:36,380
There's wonder and delay.

39
00:02:36,500 --> 00:02:41,460
And we experience these things in different ways at different times, but there's this time where God just seems so close,

40
00:02:41,460 --> 00:02:47,240
and everything's going the way that we think it should be, and it doesn't last that long.

41
00:02:47,240 --> 00:02:48,240
Right?

42
00:02:48,240 --> 00:02:49,740
For oftentimes.

43
00:02:49,740 --> 00:02:56,600
And so today, what we're going to talk about is the bottom left, where life seems good.

44
00:02:56,600 --> 00:02:58,240
The circumstances of our life are fine.

45
00:02:58,240 --> 00:03:05,200
There's nothing overwhelmingly bad in our life, and yet God still seems a little bit absent.

46
00:03:06,500 --> 00:03:09,660
I think this is going to be a hard message to preach, so we'll see how it goes.

47
00:03:09,660 --> 00:03:14,660
If you want to turn in your Bibles to Luke chapter 10, we're going to be in Luke chapter 10 first,

48
00:03:14,660 --> 00:03:18,420
and then we're going to be in a lot of Bible after that, but it'll all be on the screen.

49
00:03:18,420 --> 00:03:22,760
When Merce and I moved here, we moved here kind of like right in the height of the pandemic,

50
00:03:22,760 --> 00:03:26,440
and the housing market was ridiculous.

51
00:03:27,240 --> 00:03:33,040
It's still ridiculous, but it was pretty ridiculous, and we really couldn't find anywhere to live for the amount of money

52
00:03:33,040 --> 00:03:34,900
that we'd been pre-approved of from the bank.

53
00:03:34,900 --> 00:03:36,860
Anybody ever had that experience before?

54
00:03:36,860 --> 00:03:38,880
Especially the first house, right?

55
00:03:38,880 --> 00:03:45,180
But God kind of just, in the way in which he has always done for Merce and I, he provided.

56
00:03:45,180 --> 00:03:51,920
Through some friends of ours that go to our church, we bought their house from them for a very reasonable price.

57
00:03:52,480 --> 00:03:53,080
It was awesome.

58
00:03:53,080 --> 00:03:54,180
It was God's provision.

59
00:03:54,180 --> 00:03:54,980
It was God's hand.

60
00:03:54,980 --> 00:03:58,240
And yet there was one challenge.

61
00:03:58,240 --> 00:04:00,880
The bottom, it's the old farmhouse.

62
00:04:00,880 --> 00:04:02,300
The bottom had been totally renovated.

63
00:04:02,300 --> 00:04:05,440
The top had not been touched since like 1970.

64
00:04:05,440 --> 00:04:10,280
There was one outlet in each room, and we wanted to have a baby.

65
00:04:10,280 --> 00:04:17,560
And so putting a baby in a second-story house where there's one electrical outlet, it's not going to happen, right?

66
00:04:17,560 --> 00:04:20,500
Some of you are like, grow up.

67
00:04:22,100 --> 00:04:23,400
Toughen up, Rory.

68
00:04:23,400 --> 00:04:24,140
Get over it.

69
00:04:24,140 --> 00:04:24,700
It's fine.

70
00:04:24,700 --> 00:04:27,500
A little bit of wallpaper, a little bit of asbestos never hurt anybody.

71
00:04:27,500 --> 00:04:29,400
All right.

72
00:04:29,400 --> 00:04:37,860
So in order to renovate the upstairs, we first had to upgrade our electrical system because there wasn't enough power to upgrade the second floor.

73
00:04:37,860 --> 00:04:45,780
And again, poor person like myself, I reached out to Corey, and I'm like, you know any electricians?

74
00:04:46,300 --> 00:04:48,460
Because I'm not going to pay a real electrician.

75
00:04:48,460 --> 00:04:52,460
So if you know any like electricians, I'd love for that to happen.

76
00:04:52,460 --> 00:04:55,940
And of course, you know, if anybody knows Corey, he's always got a guy.

77
00:04:55,940 --> 00:04:59,860
So Corey had an electrical guy come to my house.

78
00:04:59,860 --> 00:05:00,580
His name is Brian.

79
00:05:00,580 --> 00:05:01,500
He's a great dude.

80
00:05:01,500 --> 00:05:02,380
Love him to death.

81
00:05:02,640 --> 00:05:07,000
And we spent all day Friday, and I'm going to say we a lot in this story, but it was mostly him.

82
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:12,100
We spent all day like working to upgrade the electrical power system.

83
00:05:12,100 --> 00:05:17,520
We had an inspector that had to come at the end of the day and approve everything so that we could flip the lights on, right?

84
00:05:18,340 --> 00:05:23,740
And so we're doing all the right things, the right way, and again, we meaning mostly him.

85
00:05:23,740 --> 00:05:25,300
I'm there.

86
00:05:25,300 --> 00:05:33,940
I dug a trench at one point, and even that, I didn't dig it as deep as I was supposed to dig it because, you know, soft hands here.

87
00:05:37,360 --> 00:05:42,860
So we did everything the right way, and he's actually, like, I call him an electrician.

88
00:05:42,860 --> 00:05:43,960
He's actually an electrician.

89
00:05:43,960 --> 00:05:44,640
He knows what he's doing.

90
00:05:44,640 --> 00:05:48,900
Everything the right way, and the inspector comes, and everything's set up perfectly.

91
00:05:48,900 --> 00:05:49,720
Brian's like, it's good.

92
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:50,180
It's good.

93
00:05:50,180 --> 00:05:51,200
Flip the switch.

94
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:53,580
No power.

95
00:05:53,580 --> 00:05:56,160
I look at him.

96
00:05:56,160 --> 00:05:56,840
He looks at me.

97
00:05:56,840 --> 00:06:05,700
We both look at the inspector, and, you know, he does the head scratch, which is never a good thing because he did everything right.

98
00:06:06,020 --> 00:06:07,440
We did all the things.

99
00:06:07,440 --> 00:06:10,720
It was all done, all the right things in all the right order.

100
00:06:10,720 --> 00:06:12,820
Flip the switch off, flip the switch back on, nothing.

101
00:06:12,820 --> 00:06:18,060
Take it apart, put it back together, real quick, scramble, flip the switch on, flip the switch off, nothing.

102
00:06:18,060 --> 00:06:22,660
It's not working, and the inspector's like, well, I got to go home.

103
00:06:22,660 --> 00:06:26,780
So you're going to have to stay in a hotel this week, and I'll see you Monday afternoon.

104
00:06:26,780 --> 00:06:28,960
And I'm like, that can't happen, right?

105
00:06:28,960 --> 00:06:34,380
So anyway, all of this to say at the very last minute, we got it all figured out.

106
00:06:34,380 --> 00:06:42,820
There was a little nail that had just pierced the external casing of the main wiring, and it had kind of disconnected the power.

107
00:06:42,820 --> 00:06:47,460
So again, everything was done the right way, in the right order, and yet there was no power.

108
00:06:48,280 --> 00:06:59,200
And I think that's the way that we experience this season often in life as Christians of bravado, the bottom left corner, where we're doing all the right things.

109
00:07:00,780 --> 00:07:03,220
We're doing all the right things the right way.

110
00:07:03,220 --> 00:07:07,580
We're doing the things we're supposed to be doing, and yet it doesn't seem like God's presence is there.

111
00:07:09,220 --> 00:07:12,420
It doesn't seem like God's power is available to us.

112
00:07:12,420 --> 00:07:14,520
Have any of us ever experienced this before?

113
00:07:14,520 --> 00:07:25,440
How frustrating can it be to do all of the right things the right way, to listen to what the pastor says, to read the Bible, to do the things, and yet not feel like God is present?

114
00:07:27,500 --> 00:07:31,680
And in my opinion, I think this is going to be—I'm super humble, obviously.

115
00:07:31,680 --> 00:07:40,400
This is going to be the hardest one of these sermons to preach, because we don't like to talk about this as Christians.

116
00:07:41,240 --> 00:07:43,300
We don't like to talk about this season in our life.

117
00:07:43,300 --> 00:07:46,700
We don't have a theological framework for it.

118
00:07:46,700 --> 00:07:52,860
We're not honest with ourselves or with others about it, because we think if we're doing the right things, God should do the thing in return.

119
00:07:52,860 --> 00:07:55,460
It's this transactional thing.

120
00:07:55,460 --> 00:07:56,740
I put in the coin.

121
00:07:56,740 --> 00:07:58,520
I should get the blessing.

122
00:07:58,520 --> 00:07:59,740
Right?

123
00:07:59,740 --> 00:08:09,140
And so when we experience the silence of God when seemingly nothing is going wrong, we don't have a framework for it.

124
00:08:09,140 --> 00:08:10,320
And sometimes we just pretend.

125
00:08:10,320 --> 00:08:10,880
We fake it.

126
00:08:10,940 --> 00:08:12,920
We say, when the pastor asks us how we're doing, we say good.

127
00:08:12,920 --> 00:08:14,020
Right?

128
00:08:14,020 --> 00:08:20,580
And for any of us that have been walking with Jesus for any time at all, we know about this season.

129
00:08:20,580 --> 00:08:25,580
We've experienced this season, especially when you get involved in ministry and you start doing work for God.

130
00:08:25,580 --> 00:08:34,260
Matt called this season, when I was talking to him about it, he said it's—it is an occupational hazard for pastors.

131
00:08:34,260 --> 00:08:36,920
It's just work has to get done.

132
00:08:36,920 --> 00:08:40,680
And so whether you feel God or not, I've got to preach a sermon next week, right?

133
00:08:41,380 --> 00:08:42,600
It's just—that's just how it is.

134
00:08:42,600 --> 00:08:43,540
That's how the sausage is made.

135
00:08:43,540 --> 00:08:43,880
I'm sorry.

136
00:08:43,880 --> 00:08:46,980
I know my friend Chris over here, wherever—where's he at?

137
00:08:46,980 --> 00:08:48,380
Chris Holmes.

138
00:08:48,380 --> 00:08:49,020
There he is.

139
00:08:49,020 --> 00:08:54,900
He thinks that, like, he has this joke where I just, like, go for a walk in the woods and God comes down and gives me a sermon.

140
00:08:55,020 --> 00:08:56,420
I really wish it happened like that.

141
00:08:56,420 --> 00:09:02,440
But sometimes there's this season of dryness and we don't feel God's presence.

142
00:09:02,440 --> 00:09:10,680
Oftentimes—and I would extend this to not just pastors but all of you who volunteer and do ministry—that there's stuff to be done for God.

143
00:09:10,940 --> 00:09:14,500
And sometimes, even when God doesn't feel present, we still feel like we have to go do it.

144
00:09:14,500 --> 00:09:17,400
We don't have a framework for this.

145
00:09:17,400 --> 00:09:27,720
And I came across this quote from Mother Teresa a few weeks before she was about to win the Nobel Peace Prize for her Christian charity.

146
00:09:28,320 --> 00:09:28,560
Right?

147
00:09:28,560 --> 00:09:30,420
So, like, that's not life is bad.

148
00:09:30,420 --> 00:09:36,340
You're doing the thing that God has called you to do so well that the entire world has stopped and looked at you and said,

149
00:09:36,340 --> 00:09:39,720
wow, you're doing the thing that God told you to do.

150
00:09:39,720 --> 00:09:43,100
And this is what Mother Teresa wrote one of her spiritual mentors at this time.

151
00:09:43,100 --> 00:09:50,460
She said, as for me, the silence and the emptiness is so great that I look and I do not see.

152
00:09:50,460 --> 00:09:52,240
I listen.

153
00:09:52,240 --> 00:09:53,880
I do not hear.

154
00:09:53,880 --> 00:09:57,700
The tongue moves but does not speak.

155
00:09:58,320 --> 00:10:03,780
I want you to pray for me that I let him have free hand.

156
00:10:03,780 --> 00:10:09,920
So, maybe you're in here and this season resonates with you.

157
00:10:09,920 --> 00:10:15,480
Maybe you're a Christian, you're a follower of Jesus, and you're in this season where there's no circumstances in your life

158
00:10:15,480 --> 00:10:21,900
that really should lead you to a point of God's absence or the feeling of God's absence, and yet you're dry.

159
00:10:21,900 --> 00:10:23,300
You're in a season of drought.

160
00:10:23,300 --> 00:10:25,440
Maybe you're here and you're a spiritual seeker.

161
00:10:25,440 --> 00:10:28,100
You're not a follower of Jesus yet, but you want to be.

162
00:10:28,100 --> 00:10:29,820
You're like, you're interested in this whole Christian thing.

163
00:10:29,820 --> 00:10:30,760
You're doing the right things.

164
00:10:30,760 --> 00:10:31,500
You're coming to church.

165
00:10:31,500 --> 00:10:31,880
You're praying.

166
00:10:31,880 --> 00:10:33,920
You're reading your Bible and nothing.

167
00:10:33,920 --> 00:10:41,100
So, how should we think about this season of our life and what should we do to respond?

168
00:10:41,100 --> 00:10:47,240
And if you're in here and this season doesn't resonate with you at all, just take notes because sometime it will.

169
00:10:47,240 --> 00:10:49,280
Do that for all of the seasons, right?

170
00:10:49,280 --> 00:10:54,900
You might not be in this season right now, but take good notes because one day you will find yourself in one of these seasons.

171
00:10:55,320 --> 00:10:59,040
So, I think there's a few reasons we might experience this season.

172
00:10:59,040 --> 00:10:59,780
I have four.

173
00:10:59,780 --> 00:11:05,100
There's probably more, but I only have so much time and I'm only smart enough to do the four.

174
00:11:05,100 --> 00:11:08,260
So, we're going to do four reasons why we might experience this.

175
00:11:08,680 --> 00:11:12,100
Let's start first in Luke chapter 10, verse 38.

176
00:11:12,100 --> 00:11:20,820
Now, as they went on their way, Jesus entered a village and a woman named Martha welcomed him into her house.

177
00:11:20,820 --> 00:11:25,040
She had a sister called Mary who sat at the Lord's feet and listened to his teaching.

178
00:11:25,160 --> 00:11:27,660
But Martha was distracted.

179
00:11:27,660 --> 00:11:29,300
Look at your neighbor and say, distracted.

180
00:11:29,300 --> 00:11:33,880
Martha was distracted with much serving.

181
00:11:33,880 --> 00:11:39,080
And she went up to him and said, Lord, do you not care that my sister has left me to serve alone?

182
00:11:39,080 --> 00:11:40,660
Tell her to help me.

183
00:11:40,660 --> 00:11:45,100
But the Lord answered her, Martha, Martha, Martha.

184
00:11:47,100 --> 00:11:52,800
You are anxious and troubled about many things, but one thing is necessary.

185
00:11:52,800 --> 00:11:57,840
And Mary has chosen the good portion, which will not be taken away from her.

186
00:11:59,580 --> 00:12:05,400
See, Martha gets a really bad rap in this passage, but I think that's kind of a little mean.

187
00:12:05,400 --> 00:12:12,300
Because this is a culture of hospitality where, like, she had guests coming to her house that needed to be taken care of.

188
00:12:12,300 --> 00:12:14,580
There was work that needed to be done.

189
00:12:14,580 --> 00:12:20,760
Like, Jesus and his disciples have been traveling a long distance in a culture where Chick-fil-A isn't just closed on Sunday.

190
00:12:20,760 --> 00:12:22,600
It's closed every day, right?

191
00:12:22,600 --> 00:12:27,400
So, they're not getting off Jerusalem exit number two to get some food.

192
00:12:27,400 --> 00:12:28,920
Like, it's like they've got nothing.

193
00:12:28,920 --> 00:12:33,640
They show up to Martha's house, and she feels this overwhelming responsibility.

194
00:12:33,640 --> 00:12:35,220
These are my guests.

195
00:12:35,220 --> 00:12:36,500
I need to take care of them.

196
00:12:36,500 --> 00:12:38,360
Someone needs to get the food ready.

197
00:12:38,360 --> 00:12:40,780
Someone needs to take care of the guests.

198
00:12:40,780 --> 00:12:46,740
And yet, Jesus is clear with Martha at the end of this passage that there is one thing.

199
00:12:46,740 --> 00:12:51,460
There is one thing that is most important, that is more important than external physical needs,

200
00:12:51,460 --> 00:12:53,640
and that is internal spiritual needs.

201
00:12:54,380 --> 00:12:58,000
See, this story comes at the end of a chapter that's really all about productivity.

202
00:12:58,000 --> 00:13:00,480
It's all about busyness and ministry.

203
00:13:00,480 --> 00:13:03,520
At the beginning of chapter 10, Jesus sends out 72 disciples.

204
00:13:03,520 --> 00:13:07,340
Two by two, he gives them authority to go out and do miracles.

205
00:13:07,340 --> 00:13:10,240
They go without him to do the work of the ministry.

206
00:13:10,240 --> 00:13:13,260
And then after that is the story of the Good Samaritan.

207
00:13:13,260 --> 00:13:15,020
I don't know if you guys know about the story of the Good Samaritan.

208
00:13:15,020 --> 00:13:17,240
The Good Samaritan is doing a lot of work.

209
00:13:17,880 --> 00:13:19,120
All kinds of work.

210
00:13:19,120 --> 00:13:24,560
It's like a busy thing for the Good Samaritan to love this person in need.

211
00:13:24,560 --> 00:13:27,540
The story comes at the end of a chapter about productivity.

212
00:13:27,540 --> 00:13:32,500
And I think this story is as much for Martha as it is for his disciples.

213
00:13:32,500 --> 00:13:38,880
It's a lesson that they all need to learn as they're about to go into a season of ministry.

214
00:13:38,880 --> 00:13:45,680
See, Jesus knows that when we get busy doing God's work, we will be overwhelmed by the needs of this world.

215
00:13:45,680 --> 00:13:51,260
There will always be things to do for God.

216
00:13:53,520 --> 00:13:57,680
Jesus wants to make sure that we know, that the disciples know, that Martha knew.

217
00:13:57,680 --> 00:14:02,680
That no matter what things have to get done, there's one thing.

218
00:14:02,680 --> 00:14:06,200
There's one thing that is the most important of all things.

219
00:14:06,200 --> 00:14:14,560
That is, the presence with God always takes priority over productivity for God.

220
00:14:14,560 --> 00:14:17,220
It's the most important commandment.

221
00:14:17,220 --> 00:14:20,100
Love the Lord your God with all of your heart, soul, mind, and strength.

222
00:14:20,100 --> 00:14:21,820
The second is like it.

223
00:14:21,820 --> 00:14:23,120
Love your neighbor as yourself.

224
00:14:23,840 --> 00:14:26,500
Some of us, we get so overwhelmed with the needs of our neighbors.

225
00:14:26,500 --> 00:14:28,360
We get so overwhelmed with the needs of ministry.

226
00:14:28,360 --> 00:14:34,580
We get so overwhelmed with the busyness of life that we spend all of our time doing the second thing.

227
00:14:34,580 --> 00:14:39,160
And we miss out on the most important thing.

228
00:14:39,160 --> 00:14:44,180
See, we live in a society that wants to define us by what we can offer society.

229
00:14:44,180 --> 00:14:50,040
The kingdom of God wants to define you by who you are in relationship to God.

230
00:14:51,800 --> 00:14:55,060
You are a beloved son or daughter of God.

231
00:14:55,060 --> 00:14:55,600
Listen to this.

232
00:14:55,720 --> 00:15:08,160
God's love for us, his presence in our life, is not dependent on what we bring to the table.

233
00:15:08,160 --> 00:15:11,580
It's dependent on him who brought us to the table.

234
00:15:11,580 --> 00:15:14,740
Jesus has brought us to the table with his faithfulness.

235
00:15:15,540 --> 00:15:19,440
I think it's easy for us to get distracted by ministry opportunities around us.

236
00:15:19,440 --> 00:15:23,760
That we forget the very reason we started doing ministry in the first place.

237
00:15:23,760 --> 00:15:28,940
And that's because we had an encounter with the living God who loved us, who gave himself for us.

238
00:15:28,940 --> 00:15:37,800
We had this season of wonder and delight where we fell in love with the God who gave his very own son to die for us.

239
00:15:37,800 --> 00:15:39,660
There's speaking of very own sons.

240
00:15:39,820 --> 00:15:40,220
There he is.

241
00:15:40,220 --> 00:15:51,820
And then we get busy doing what we're called to do because of what he's done for us.

242
00:15:51,820 --> 00:15:54,380
It starts out good, but we get distracted.

243
00:15:54,380 --> 00:15:57,600
We get lost in the busyness of ministry.

244
00:15:57,600 --> 00:15:59,180
And look at this.

245
00:15:59,180 --> 00:16:00,520
This is what I love about this story.

246
00:16:02,900 --> 00:16:06,100
Was the presence of God absent from Martha in this story?

247
00:16:06,100 --> 00:16:09,140
No, he's just in the other room.

248
00:16:09,140 --> 00:16:10,740
Right?

249
00:16:10,740 --> 00:16:17,500
He's literally in the other room and she's like, she's so busy doing ministry that she misses out on the presence of God.

250
00:16:17,500 --> 00:16:22,920
And I can't help but wonder if some of us don't find ourselves in this season of life where we feel like God is absent.

251
00:16:22,920 --> 00:16:25,620
Where are you?

252
00:16:25,620 --> 00:16:27,900
And it's not that he's absent.

253
00:16:28,840 --> 00:16:31,020
It's just that we're too distracted to see him.

254
00:16:31,020 --> 00:16:35,380
We're too distracted prioritizing our productivity over the presence of God.

255
00:16:35,380 --> 00:16:42,000
And what if God is using this feeling of absence in your life to help you see that you've taken your eyes off of your first priority?

256
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:47,460
What if God is calling you to take off your apron and sit at the feet of Jesus?

257
00:16:47,460 --> 00:16:54,180
So, I think it's important that we take this warning seriously.

258
00:16:54,180 --> 00:16:58,400
I take this warning very seriously for us as a church, especially for our volunteers and our staff.

259
00:16:58,460 --> 00:16:59,800
You guys know the stats.

260
00:16:59,800 --> 00:17:00,380
Maybe you don't.

261
00:17:00,380 --> 00:17:01,120
I know the stats.

262
00:17:01,120 --> 00:17:05,380
That 20% of the people do 100% of the work in churches.

263
00:17:05,380 --> 00:17:11,300
I don't want you, those of you who are bought-in volunteers who serve all the time,

264
00:17:11,300 --> 00:17:17,060
I don't want you doing so much ministry that you get burnt out and that you don't experience the presence of God in your life.

265
00:17:17,060 --> 00:17:22,700
We say no to things all the time as a church because I do not want our staff being burnt out from ministry

266
00:17:22,700 --> 00:17:25,360
and not having time to sit in the presence of God.

267
00:17:26,980 --> 00:17:29,360
This is important to me for our church.

268
00:17:29,360 --> 00:17:37,060
I say it's important to me for my life, but I don't always do it that well, right?

269
00:17:37,060 --> 00:17:40,940
Sometimes I build intentional margin into my life for the presence of God,

270
00:17:40,940 --> 00:17:45,260
and instead of using that intentional margin that I built for the presence of God,

271
00:17:45,260 --> 00:17:48,240
to sit in the presence of God, guess what I use it for?

272
00:17:48,240 --> 00:17:50,960
Oh, man.

273
00:17:50,960 --> 00:17:53,620
You preach the rest of the sermon.

274
00:17:53,620 --> 00:17:54,120
I'm out here.

275
00:17:54,120 --> 00:17:56,880
He said the masters.

276
00:17:56,880 --> 00:17:57,420
Wow.

277
00:17:57,420 --> 00:17:58,600
That is true.

278
00:17:59,280 --> 00:18:05,420
But oftentimes, I literally, I create this margin and I sit around worrying about the things that I should be doing

279
00:18:05,420 --> 00:18:07,740
instead of sitting in the presence of God.

280
00:18:07,740 --> 00:18:12,840
Anybody else get so distracted with all of the overwhelming needs of ministry

281
00:18:12,840 --> 00:18:16,820
that even when you take a break, you can't think about anything else except for what needs to be done?

282
00:18:16,820 --> 00:18:19,620
All right.

283
00:18:19,620 --> 00:18:19,980
Cool.

284
00:18:21,620 --> 00:18:26,180
Listen to what Jesus writes to the church in Revelation chapter 2.

285
00:18:26,180 --> 00:18:31,680
This is the church at Ephesus, I believe.

286
00:18:32,540 --> 00:18:36,440
I know your deeds, your hard work, your perseverance.

287
00:18:36,440 --> 00:18:38,300
How does it sound like the church at Ephesus is doing?

288
00:18:38,300 --> 00:18:40,480
Good, right?

289
00:18:40,480 --> 00:18:45,280
If we're American Christianity, man, the church at Ephesus, God knows their deeds.

290
00:18:45,280 --> 00:18:46,760
He knows their hard work.

291
00:18:46,760 --> 00:18:47,820
He knows their perseverance.

292
00:18:47,820 --> 00:18:50,920
Like that is all of the American buzzwords.

293
00:18:50,920 --> 00:18:52,000
They are crushing it.

294
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:55,260
You have persevered.

295
00:18:55,260 --> 00:18:59,620
You have endured hardships for my name and have not grown weary yet.

296
00:19:01,060 --> 00:19:02,460
I hold this against you.

297
00:19:02,460 --> 00:19:07,500
You have forsaken the love you had at first.

298
00:19:07,500 --> 00:19:12,020
Does that sound like American Christianity?

299
00:19:12,020 --> 00:19:18,020
We get so busy doing the things that we think we're supposed to do.

300
00:19:18,020 --> 00:19:20,580
Persevering, not getting weary.

301
00:19:20,580 --> 00:19:23,860
I know so many of you in this room who work so hard for the kingdom.

302
00:19:23,860 --> 00:19:25,820
And you're not weary.

303
00:19:25,820 --> 00:19:29,940
And when you are weary, you get mad at yourself and you stand back up and you keep going.

304
00:19:31,060 --> 00:19:36,840
Let's make sure, even in our faithfulness to ministry, that we don't forsake our first love.

305
00:19:36,840 --> 00:19:42,600
That we make time to sit at the feet of Jesus in the presence of Jesus.

306
00:19:42,600 --> 00:19:45,140
That we minister out of the overflow.

307
00:19:46,580 --> 00:19:49,920
Is it possible you're experiencing this season of God feeling absent?

308
00:19:49,920 --> 00:19:53,580
Not because he is, but because you're too distracted to acknowledge him.

309
00:19:53,580 --> 00:20:02,380
My desire for myself and for our church is that we would be a people who intentionally prioritize the presence of God over our productivity.

310
00:20:03,420 --> 00:20:08,040
That we do ministry, not from an empty tank, but overflowing out of the heart of love for God.

311
00:20:08,040 --> 00:20:08,660
Here's the thing.

312
00:20:08,660 --> 00:20:15,040
If you do ministry out of a sense of guilt or necessity,

313
00:20:15,040 --> 00:20:20,420
do you think anybody in that room was happy to be served by Martha that day?

314
00:20:20,420 --> 00:20:27,480
Do you think anybody in that room thought Martha was serving because she wanted to?

315
00:20:28,880 --> 00:20:33,200
No, she's running around, huffing and puffing, stomping her feet, rolling her eyes.

316
00:20:33,200 --> 00:20:34,580
Here's what happens.

317
00:20:34,580 --> 00:20:38,200
When we don't serve out of the overflow, when we serve because we feel like we have to,

318
00:20:38,200 --> 00:20:42,820
when we serve out of necessity, the people that we're serving know that we don't even want to serve them.

319
00:20:42,820 --> 00:20:51,160
We've got to serve out of the overflow so that they can experience the presence of God that we've experienced.

320
00:20:51,160 --> 00:20:55,080
So that they're not being served by somebody who's just doing it because they feel like they have to,

321
00:20:55,160 --> 00:21:01,800
but they're serving by, they're being served by someone who loves them, wants to serve them.

322
00:21:01,800 --> 00:21:03,360
All right.

323
00:21:03,360 --> 00:21:08,340
Reason number two, that we can experience God's absence in our life,

324
00:21:08,340 --> 00:21:17,560
even when things are going well, is because maybe we're not fully surrendered to God.

325
00:21:18,120 --> 00:21:26,220
Matthew chapter 16, whoever wants to be my disciple must deny themselves, take up their cross and follow me.

326
00:21:26,220 --> 00:21:31,720
For whoever wants to save their life will lose it, but whoever loses their life for my sake will find it.

327
00:21:31,720 --> 00:21:37,040
What good will it be for someone to gain the whole world and yet forfeit their soul?

328
00:21:37,040 --> 00:21:41,180
Or what can anyone give in exchange for their soul?

329
00:21:43,020 --> 00:21:46,860
See, I think a lot of us who might be experiencing this season of our life,

330
00:21:46,860 --> 00:21:49,680
we started our journey of faith with total surrender.

331
00:21:49,680 --> 00:21:53,060
We had this encounter with the living God and we were like,

332
00:21:53,060 --> 00:21:54,920
look, everything else, nothing else matters.

333
00:21:54,920 --> 00:21:55,920
It's all at your feet.

334
00:21:55,920 --> 00:21:57,060
I'm totally surrendered.

335
00:21:57,060 --> 00:21:59,600
I want to follow you with everything that I have.

336
00:21:59,600 --> 00:22:05,600
But over time, we started to take a piece here, a piece here.

337
00:22:05,940 --> 00:22:09,000
And that total surrender is like kind of partial surrender at this point.

338
00:22:09,000 --> 00:22:18,440
It's like, it's like we treat God like our friends who are house guests.

339
00:22:18,440 --> 00:22:21,700
We invite them in and we say, what do we say?

340
00:22:21,700 --> 00:22:24,060
Make yourselves at home, right?

341
00:22:24,060 --> 00:22:27,560
I've got some really good, multiple really good friends at this church.

342
00:22:27,560 --> 00:22:32,180
Actually, three sets of good friends at this church who invite me over to their home regularly,

343
00:22:32,180 --> 00:22:34,360
who I have door codes to their house.

344
00:22:34,780 --> 00:22:35,720
They love me so much.

345
00:22:35,720 --> 00:22:38,260
It's like, let yourself in, even when I'm not around.

346
00:22:38,260 --> 00:22:40,360
But here's what I know to be true.

347
00:22:40,360 --> 00:22:41,460
At least I think this is true.

348
00:22:41,460 --> 00:22:44,500
If they're home when I let myself in with the door code,

349
00:22:44,500 --> 00:22:50,520
and I start like randomly just going up to their bedroom and opening up their dresser drawers,

350
00:22:50,520 --> 00:22:54,960
they're like, what are you doing, dude?

351
00:22:54,960 --> 00:22:57,920
I'm like, you said make myself at home.

352
00:22:57,920 --> 00:23:00,000
I'm just making myself at home.

353
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:03,560
It's like, yeah, that's not what I meant, right?

354
00:23:04,120 --> 00:23:07,780
And so I think sometimes this is kind of how we treat God.

355
00:23:07,780 --> 00:23:09,000
We're like, hey, God, make yourself at home.

356
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:09,680
Totally surrendered.

357
00:23:09,680 --> 00:23:10,860
What's mine is yours.

358
00:23:10,860 --> 00:23:12,900
You make yourself at home.

359
00:23:12,900 --> 00:23:15,180
You go into any room you want, open up any drawer you want,

360
00:23:15,180 --> 00:23:16,940
until he starts doing it.

361
00:23:16,940 --> 00:23:20,160
We're like, that?

362
00:23:20,160 --> 00:23:21,360
You want that?

363
00:23:21,360 --> 00:23:23,660
You're going to ask me to give up that?

364
00:23:23,660 --> 00:23:26,220
I've got to surrender that thing?

365
00:23:28,040 --> 00:23:30,080
No, no, never mind.

366
00:23:30,080 --> 00:23:32,180
I'm going to close the door to this room.

367
00:23:32,180 --> 00:23:34,680
Make yourself at home, except for this room.

368
00:23:34,680 --> 00:23:36,000
Right?

369
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:41,560
And if we're not careful, we end up like sectioning off entire wings of the house to the Lord,

370
00:23:41,560 --> 00:23:43,240
hardening our hearts.

371
00:23:43,800 --> 00:23:51,740
And essentially, we justify it because we're like, well, we gave him like, he's got a lot of room in here.

372
00:23:51,740 --> 00:23:54,700
This is a big house.

373
00:23:54,700 --> 00:23:57,380
He's got a lot of access to a lot of things.

374
00:23:57,380 --> 00:23:58,160
What does this say?

375
00:23:59,460 --> 00:24:02,520
We deny themselves, their entire selves.

376
00:24:02,520 --> 00:24:04,560
We have to be totally surrendered to God.

377
00:24:04,560 --> 00:24:08,160
And yet, we wall off the doors of our house.

378
00:24:08,160 --> 00:24:10,840
Don't touch this area of addiction.

379
00:24:10,840 --> 00:24:13,180
Don't touch this area of unforgiveness.

380
00:24:13,180 --> 00:24:14,700
Don't touch this relationship.

381
00:24:14,700 --> 00:24:16,860
Don't ask me to give up the masters.

382
00:24:16,860 --> 00:24:19,260
Don't do it.

383
00:24:19,260 --> 00:24:20,600
That's the one room, right?

384
00:24:20,600 --> 00:24:21,500
It's a religious holiday.

385
00:24:21,500 --> 00:24:29,160
So, I think some of us, we're experiencing God's absence in our life

386
00:24:29,160 --> 00:24:33,180
because we've stopped letting him have access to certain parts of our lives.

387
00:24:33,180 --> 00:24:38,120
He feels absent to us because we're spending most of our times in the rooms

388
00:24:38,120 --> 00:24:39,780
that we aren't giving him access to.

389
00:24:39,780 --> 00:24:41,800
God, where are you?

390
00:24:41,800 --> 00:24:45,960
He's like, hey, you closed the door.

391
00:24:45,960 --> 00:24:49,220
I'm right outside.

392
00:24:49,220 --> 00:24:51,840
I'm not absent from you.

393
00:24:51,840 --> 00:24:55,520
You just went into the room that you told me I wasn't allowed to be in and closed it.

394
00:24:56,380 --> 00:25:00,880
And this is what, this is what Jesus says to another church in Revelation.

395
00:25:00,880 --> 00:25:03,540
He says, I know your deeds.

396
00:25:03,540 --> 00:25:05,540
You're neither hot nor cold.

397
00:25:05,540 --> 00:25:06,800
Not fully surrendered.

398
00:25:06,800 --> 00:25:09,220
I wish you were either one or the other.

399
00:25:09,220 --> 00:25:13,800
So, because you're lukewarm, you're neither hot nor cold, I'm about to spit you out of my mouth.

400
00:25:16,600 --> 00:25:17,400
But listen to this.

401
00:25:17,400 --> 00:25:18,060
This is good news.

402
00:25:18,060 --> 00:25:19,340
I know that sounds like bad news.

403
00:25:19,340 --> 00:25:24,280
And if you grew up in church at all, this verse has been used to make you feel like a terrible person many times.

404
00:25:24,280 --> 00:25:28,340
And I don't want that to happen this morning because what I want you to see here is, listen to this,

405
00:25:28,420 --> 00:25:36,900
those whom I love, I rebuke, I discipline, I love you so much, I'm not going to let you wall yourself off in these rooms without me.

406
00:25:36,900 --> 00:25:38,360
I want to be with you.

407
00:25:38,360 --> 00:25:45,800
And so, if there's situations in your life where you're kind of walling God off, listen to this this morning.

408
00:25:46,340 --> 00:25:49,160
I stand at the door and knock.

409
00:25:49,160 --> 00:25:51,480
I'm right outside.

410
00:25:51,480 --> 00:25:55,380
If you feel like I'm absent to you, just know I'm right outside the door knocking.

411
00:25:55,380 --> 00:25:56,660
All you have to do is let me in.

412
00:25:56,660 --> 00:26:02,380
If anyone hears my voice and opens the door, I will come in this morning.

413
00:26:02,380 --> 00:26:08,080
Is it possible that you're experiencing the absence of God because you have had certain areas of your life

414
00:26:08,080 --> 00:26:10,440
where you've kind of said, nope, don't touch that.

415
00:26:13,040 --> 00:26:17,620
And God knows for your good and for his glory, he's got to have access to it.

416
00:26:17,620 --> 00:26:23,600
Might not feel good at first, but it always leads to abundant life.

417
00:26:23,600 --> 00:26:29,720
Is it possible you're distracted from God's presence because of your unwillingness to surrender parts of your life to him?

418
00:26:29,720 --> 00:26:30,680
He loves you too much.

419
00:26:30,680 --> 00:26:31,600
He's going to keep knocking.

420
00:26:31,600 --> 00:26:32,680
He's going to keep asking.

421
00:26:32,680 --> 00:26:39,060
I was talking to a friend about that this week, and I was just going through my outline,

422
00:26:39,060 --> 00:26:41,160
and she said, wow, you know what?

423
00:26:41,580 --> 00:26:44,360
I experienced this before in my life, but it wasn't conscious.

424
00:26:44,360 --> 00:26:45,120
It was subconscious.

425
00:26:45,120 --> 00:26:50,080
She said there was this area in her life that had become so important to her

426
00:26:50,080 --> 00:26:54,520
that she wasn't like rebellingly saying, no, God, you can't have this.

427
00:26:54,520 --> 00:26:58,840
It had just become so important to her that she was kind of distancing herself from God

428
00:26:58,840 --> 00:27:03,280
because she knew she didn't want God to meddle with this thing, right?

429
00:27:03,280 --> 00:27:04,300
It wasn't even a bad thing.

430
00:27:04,300 --> 00:27:06,800
It was a good thing, but she didn't want God to meddle with this thing.

431
00:27:06,800 --> 00:27:13,260
And so I can't help but wonder, maybe we're even subconsciously distancing ourself from God

432
00:27:13,260 --> 00:27:16,040
because we have this thing, and we're like, don't touch this thing.

433
00:27:16,040 --> 00:27:18,080
I don't want you to touch this thing.

434
00:27:18,080 --> 00:27:21,720
Reminds me of the Chronicles of Narnia.

435
00:27:21,720 --> 00:27:24,760
There's a story, a little boy named Eustace.

436
00:27:24,760 --> 00:27:25,760
Anybody know this story?

437
00:27:25,760 --> 00:27:26,740
Dragon scales.

438
00:27:26,740 --> 00:27:29,280
It's a pretty popular Christian story.

439
00:27:30,660 --> 00:27:31,980
He's being selfish.

440
00:27:31,980 --> 00:27:34,020
He ends up turning into a dragon.

441
00:27:34,020 --> 00:27:36,260
He tries to get the scales of the dragon off.

442
00:27:36,260 --> 00:27:38,220
They come off for a little bit.

443
00:27:38,220 --> 00:27:40,380
They grow back, come off, grow back.

444
00:27:40,380 --> 00:27:43,020
He's trying to handle this whole situation himself.

445
00:27:43,020 --> 00:27:48,820
And eventually Aslan shows up and says, hey, if you want those scales off,

446
00:27:48,820 --> 00:27:51,380
you've got to let me do it.

447
00:27:51,380 --> 00:27:54,520
Listen to this quote from C.S. Lewis, Chronicles of Narnia.

448
00:27:54,520 --> 00:27:56,620
He says, you will have to let me undress you.

449
00:27:56,620 --> 00:27:59,420
Eustace says, I was afraid of his claws.

450
00:27:59,840 --> 00:28:02,040
I can tell you, but I was pretty nearly desperate now.

451
00:28:02,040 --> 00:28:04,900
So I just lay flat on my back, and I let him do it.

452
00:28:04,900 --> 00:28:12,320
So, maybe we've experienced the absence of God to the point where we're desperate.

453
00:28:12,320 --> 00:28:17,860
Total surrender looks like laying on the back and just letting him do it.

454
00:28:17,860 --> 00:28:23,540
It's not always going to feel good in the moment, but it always leads to abundant life.

455
00:28:23,540 --> 00:28:29,680
All right, reason number three, that God might seem absent to us even while life is good.

456
00:28:29,840 --> 00:28:33,420
This one's probably the most obvious.

457
00:28:33,420 --> 00:28:35,540
This is probably the one you thought I was going to start with.

458
00:28:35,540 --> 00:28:41,400
Is it possible that we're ignoring an area of unrepentant sin in our life?

459
00:28:41,400 --> 00:28:43,380
Right?

460
00:28:43,380 --> 00:28:44,100
Is that possible?

461
00:28:44,100 --> 00:28:50,500
Here's the reason why I think that we don't deal with this issue very well.

462
00:28:50,900 --> 00:28:54,340
The most famous example of this in the Scriptures is a guy by the name of King David.

463
00:28:54,340 --> 00:28:55,020
Anybody know him?

464
00:28:55,020 --> 00:28:57,340
What did King David do that was wrong?

465
00:28:57,340 --> 00:29:00,720
Yeah, let's do the highlights real quick.

466
00:29:00,720 --> 00:29:01,420
Hit me with the highlights.

467
00:29:01,420 --> 00:29:04,320
Murder, adultery.

468
00:29:04,320 --> 00:29:05,820
Is that good enough?

469
00:29:06,960 --> 00:29:10,120
Okay, so David has a season of his life.

470
00:29:10,120 --> 00:29:10,820
He's the king.

471
00:29:10,820 --> 00:29:14,180
Things are still going pretty well for David, right?

472
00:29:14,180 --> 00:29:18,180
Lives in a palace, wives, concubines, food, drink.

473
00:29:18,180 --> 00:29:22,460
Nothing really too bad in his circumstances at some points in his life.

474
00:29:22,460 --> 00:29:25,660
And yet he has done these terrible things.

475
00:29:25,660 --> 00:29:28,000
He has not come to God with these things.

476
00:29:29,040 --> 00:29:30,860
And so there's this absence between him and God.

477
00:29:30,860 --> 00:29:34,640
He gets confronted and he writes this Psalm 51, verses 10 through 12.

478
00:29:34,640 --> 00:29:35,340
He says to God,

479
00:29:35,340 --> 00:29:38,400
Create in me a pure heart, O God, and renew a steadfast spirit within me.

480
00:29:38,400 --> 00:29:41,980
Do not cast your presence from me or take your Holy Spirit from me.

481
00:29:41,980 --> 00:29:42,620
Listen to this.

482
00:29:42,620 --> 00:29:46,960
Restore to me the joy or the delight of your salvation.

483
00:29:46,960 --> 00:29:50,520
Grant me a willing spirit to sustain it.

484
00:29:50,520 --> 00:29:53,800
He wants back to the season of wonder and delight.

485
00:29:53,800 --> 00:29:55,300
He knows that he's messed up.

486
00:29:55,300 --> 00:29:58,760
He knows that he's done wrong and that he knows that he needs to repent.

487
00:29:59,740 --> 00:30:04,920
And yet I feel like we don't think that this is what's going on in our life.

488
00:30:04,920 --> 00:30:11,260
Because the most famous example is so audacious, so morally impure.

489
00:30:11,260 --> 00:30:13,200
Here's what we do, I think.

490
00:30:13,200 --> 00:30:14,800
Pastorally, this is what I think.

491
00:30:14,800 --> 00:30:19,100
I think we think, well, I mean, I didn't murder anybody.

492
00:30:19,100 --> 00:30:22,080
I didn't commit adultery.

493
00:30:22,080 --> 00:30:25,360
I mean, I'm not that bad of a guy.

494
00:30:26,520 --> 00:30:30,480
Is God really, like, letting me experience this absence because of my sin?

495
00:30:30,480 --> 00:30:33,440
Because I'm holding on to some things?

496
00:30:33,440 --> 00:30:40,040
Is my unwillingness to forgive that person really that bad?

497
00:30:40,040 --> 00:30:47,000
Is my pattern of gossip at work really something that God's not a fan of?

498
00:30:47,780 --> 00:30:49,160
My lack of generosity?

499
00:30:49,160 --> 00:30:50,820
My holding on to my stuff?

500
00:30:50,820 --> 00:30:56,100
My infrequent substance abuse that I explain away as just a social thing?

501
00:30:56,100 --> 00:31:07,520
Whatever it is in your life that the Holy Spirit has clearly made known to you as an area of sin and you have made excuses for,

502
00:31:08,600 --> 00:31:15,240
is it possible that the reason you're experiencing this seemingly absence from God is because he's told you,

503
00:31:15,240 --> 00:31:17,200
look, I need to deal with this.

504
00:31:17,200 --> 00:31:20,960
And you're like, nah, it's not that bad.

505
00:31:20,960 --> 00:31:22,040
It's not adultery.

506
00:31:22,040 --> 00:31:22,620
It's not murder.

507
00:31:22,620 --> 00:31:24,620
It's fine.

508
00:31:27,180 --> 00:31:28,460
Man, here's the thing.

509
00:31:28,460 --> 00:31:34,840
I think I'm going to just let the Holy Spirit do whatever it wants to do with all of your stuff,

510
00:31:34,840 --> 00:31:39,420
but I'm going to hyper-focus on one that I think Christians do really bad at in our culture,

511
00:31:39,420 --> 00:31:40,740
and specifically even in our church.

512
00:31:40,740 --> 00:31:43,200
Unforgiveness.

513
00:31:43,200 --> 00:31:47,660
I think some of us have unforgiveness in our hearts.

514
00:31:47,660 --> 00:31:49,120
And here's the deal.

515
00:31:49,120 --> 00:31:56,860
Some of us have been deeply wounded, like legitimate bad stuff has happened to us.

516
00:31:56,860 --> 00:31:58,880
We've been betrayed.

517
00:31:58,880 --> 00:32:00,420
We've been taken advantage of.

518
00:32:00,420 --> 00:32:01,360
We've been abused.

519
00:32:01,360 --> 00:32:03,840
Whatever it might be.

520
00:32:03,840 --> 00:32:07,860
And we're holding on to the seed of unforgiveness.

521
00:32:07,860 --> 00:32:12,200
And we're justifying it because that person doesn't deserve our forgiveness.

522
00:32:12,200 --> 00:32:19,100
And I can't help but wonder if God isn't allowing you to feel a little bit of distance between him and himself

523
00:32:19,100 --> 00:32:22,220
because he wants you to see that you have been forgiven of much,

524
00:32:22,220 --> 00:32:24,040
and he requires you to forgive much.

525
00:32:24,040 --> 00:32:29,720
All throughout the Scriptures, there's clear examples.

526
00:32:29,720 --> 00:32:32,100
It's the parable of the unforgiving servant.

527
00:32:32,100 --> 00:32:34,880
It's the servant that's been forgiven of so much,

528
00:32:34,880 --> 00:32:36,700
and then he goes out and won't forgive anybody else.

529
00:32:36,700 --> 00:32:45,640
There's a—yeah, just think about that.

530
00:32:45,640 --> 00:32:46,940
Is it possible?

531
00:32:47,620 --> 00:32:49,400
And here's what forgiveness doesn't mean.

532
00:32:49,400 --> 00:32:54,440
Forgiveness doesn't mean that you give the person who hurt you total access back into your life with no boundaries.

533
00:32:58,900 --> 00:33:06,620
But man, if we spit and mock in the face of the God who created us, and he sends his one and only son,

534
00:33:06,620 --> 00:33:12,560
he generously gives his one and only son to die on behalf of our sins.

535
00:33:14,360 --> 00:33:17,700
I think we can get to a point where we can extend forgiveness to others.

536
00:33:17,700 --> 00:33:18,700
It might not happen overnight.

537
00:33:18,700 --> 00:33:22,720
I've had a season where it took me months, nine, ten months to forgive somebody.

538
00:33:22,720 --> 00:33:27,640
I'm not saying it has to happen right now, but I'm just saying if you're unwilling to even consider it,

539
00:33:28,640 --> 00:33:31,380
I don't think God's going to honor that.

540
00:33:31,380 --> 00:33:32,000
Okay.

541
00:33:32,000 --> 00:33:33,780
Reason number four.

542
00:33:33,780 --> 00:33:39,020
How much time do I have?

543
00:33:39,020 --> 00:33:39,420
Oh, crap.

544
00:33:39,420 --> 00:33:39,680
Okay.

545
00:33:42,800 --> 00:33:48,620
I think the fourth and final reason why God seems absent, this one's the most hard for us to grapple with.

546
00:33:48,620 --> 00:33:52,080
It's the hardest for us to comprehend.

547
00:33:57,880 --> 00:33:59,820
Because I think we can understand the other three.

548
00:33:59,820 --> 00:34:00,920
I think we get it.

549
00:34:00,920 --> 00:34:02,940
There's like, okay, that makes sense.

550
00:34:02,940 --> 00:34:09,580
But I think sometimes God allows us to feel his absence, not because we have anything we need to fix,

551
00:34:09,580 --> 00:34:13,340
not because we've done anything wrong, but just because he's inviting us to deeper maturity.

552
00:34:13,340 --> 00:34:16,100
He's inviting us to deeper intimacy.

553
00:34:16,100 --> 00:34:20,820
See, Mers and I, a couple weeks ago, we started weaning Rory off of his formula.

554
00:34:20,820 --> 00:34:27,440
And it's funny, we still had it up on the stovetop where we keep it.

555
00:34:27,880 --> 00:34:29,360
We hadn't thought about it very much.

556
00:34:29,360 --> 00:34:33,720
And so we're trying to get him off of formula and get him onto real food.

557
00:34:33,720 --> 00:34:37,360
He's sitting in his high chair eating real food, at least thinking about eating real food.

558
00:34:37,360 --> 00:34:39,600
And we saw him go for a piece of real food.

559
00:34:39,600 --> 00:34:43,060
And he looked up, and I swear to you, I saw him make eye contact with this formula container.

560
00:34:43,060 --> 00:34:50,300
And he goes, he's like, more formula, more formula, right?

561
00:34:50,300 --> 00:34:54,360
And like, doesn't that make sense?

562
00:34:55,320 --> 00:35:02,140
His whole life, formula has sustained him, has given him everything that he needed his whole life.

563
00:35:02,140 --> 00:35:03,820
And now I'm saying, you can't have this.

564
00:35:03,820 --> 00:35:11,820
And so we literally had to hide it because I didn't want him to look at the formula and be like, I'm not eating this.

565
00:35:11,820 --> 00:35:13,620
I almost choked three times.

566
00:35:13,620 --> 00:35:14,320
Give me the formula.

567
00:35:16,240 --> 00:35:21,880
And so it was the most loving thing that Marissa and I could do to take that thing away from him for a season.

568
00:35:23,140 --> 00:35:25,720
So that he could get a taste of macaroni and cheese.

569
00:35:25,720 --> 00:35:27,600
Right?

570
00:35:27,600 --> 00:35:33,440
And change his mind and realize, oh, like sometimes there's certain things we need in certain seasons of life.

571
00:35:33,440 --> 00:35:36,640
But we need to grow deeper and more mature.

572
00:35:36,640 --> 00:35:42,360
And I think sometimes those of us who have been followers of Jesus for a while, we keep going back to the thing that we did at first.

573
00:35:43,340 --> 00:35:47,640
And God's calling us to deeper maturity, to deeper intimacy.

574
00:35:47,640 --> 00:35:54,680
I think sometimes God allows us to feel his absence in order to invite us to grow deeper.

575
00:35:54,680 --> 00:36:00,400
Because I think the best example of this in Scripture, this was really hard for me to find scriptural evidence for.

576
00:36:00,400 --> 00:36:02,420
I even yelled at Matt a little bit.

577
00:36:02,420 --> 00:36:05,320
I'm like, you made me preach a sermon and there's, where's it at in the Bible, dude?

578
00:36:05,320 --> 00:36:08,200
You gave me this quadrant, this picture.

579
00:36:08,200 --> 00:36:09,700
I need to see it in the Bible.

580
00:36:09,700 --> 00:36:10,400
I gave him a hard time.

581
00:36:10,400 --> 00:36:12,280
And then, you know, he gave me a hard time.

582
00:36:12,280 --> 00:36:12,580
It's fine.

583
00:36:13,640 --> 00:36:15,640
John 16, Jesus said to his disciples,

584
00:36:15,640 --> 00:36:19,480
Very truly, I tell you, it is good for you that I am going away.

585
00:36:19,480 --> 00:36:22,580
Unless I go away, the advocate will not come.

586
00:36:22,580 --> 00:36:24,060
But if I go, I will send him to you.

587
00:36:24,060 --> 00:36:30,360
See, the disciples could not fathom how Jesus, his presence leaving them for a season could be good at all.

588
00:36:30,360 --> 00:36:32,800
They were in this season of wonder and delight.

589
00:36:32,800 --> 00:36:34,240
They're walking away with the Messiah.

590
00:36:34,240 --> 00:36:36,200
They're walking with the Messiah on earth.

591
00:36:36,200 --> 00:36:38,520
They're watching him heal blind people.

592
00:36:38,520 --> 00:36:39,520
They're watching.

593
00:36:39,520 --> 00:36:41,440
They literally, Peter got to walk on water.

594
00:36:41,440 --> 00:36:43,660
He's like, okay, you're leaving and that's good for me?

595
00:36:43,660 --> 00:36:47,420
But then Pentecost comes.

596
00:36:47,420 --> 00:36:49,780
Everybody's filled with the Spirit of God.

597
00:36:49,780 --> 00:36:50,720
They start prophesying.

598
00:36:50,720 --> 00:36:52,160
Everybody starts healing people.

599
00:36:54,540 --> 00:36:59,660
It's like, okay, I can see how God's absence for this season might have been for my good.

600
00:36:59,660 --> 00:37:03,080
And this is what the disciples, after the resurrection, Jesus shows up a little bit.

601
00:37:03,080 --> 00:37:04,780
But then he's gone and the Spirit hasn't come yet.

602
00:37:04,780 --> 00:37:07,680
And there's this season where they're kind of discontent and confused.

603
00:37:07,680 --> 00:37:08,520
What's going on here?

604
00:37:10,300 --> 00:37:16,980
I think it's God inviting them to grow in their faith, to mature in their faith, to trust him, even when they can't see it.

605
00:37:18,040 --> 00:37:26,040
So if you're here and you feel like life is good, God's absent, and none of the other reasons are resonating with you, you're like, nope, no sin.

606
00:37:26,040 --> 00:37:28,860
Everything's fully surrendered.

607
00:37:28,860 --> 00:37:30,080
I'm great.

608
00:37:30,080 --> 00:37:34,260
And maybe God is just inviting you to pursue him deeper.

609
00:37:35,100 --> 00:37:40,980
Hebrews 11 says, now faith is the confidence in what we hope for and the assurance about what we do not see.

610
00:37:40,980 --> 00:37:43,860
This feeling of absence allows us to grow in our faith.

611
00:37:43,860 --> 00:37:44,520
We can't see it.

612
00:37:44,520 --> 00:37:45,220
We can't feel it.

613
00:37:45,220 --> 00:37:46,540
And yet we continue to trust him.

614
00:37:46,540 --> 00:37:52,180
So how do we respond in these seasons?

615
00:37:52,180 --> 00:37:54,140
Oh, I got to hurry.

616
00:37:54,140 --> 00:37:55,080
Okay, Psalm 1-3.

617
00:37:55,080 --> 00:37:56,660
Listen to this.

618
00:37:56,660 --> 00:38:03,280
Blessed is the one who does not walk in the step of the wicked, or stand in the way of sinners, or sit in the company of mockers,

619
00:38:03,340 --> 00:38:06,520
but his delight is in the law of the Lord, who meditates on the law day and night.

620
00:38:06,520 --> 00:38:12,140
This person is like a tree planted by streams of water, which yields its fruit in season, and whose leaf does not wither.

621
00:38:12,140 --> 00:38:15,180
Whatever they do prospers.

622
00:38:15,180 --> 00:38:22,360
So, as we conclude, I'd love for you to consider those first three areas.

623
00:38:22,360 --> 00:38:26,380
Is it possible that you're experiencing God's absence because you're distracted by ministry?

624
00:38:26,380 --> 00:38:29,780
You're too busy doing all of the things, and you don't have time to sit at God's feet?

625
00:38:29,780 --> 00:38:31,120
Is it possible?

626
00:38:32,340 --> 00:38:36,620
Is it possible that you're not fully surrendering to him?

627
00:38:36,620 --> 00:38:39,600
You're certain doors in your house, you're closed off.

628
00:38:39,600 --> 00:38:41,360
And you're like, nah, I'm good.

629
00:38:41,360 --> 00:38:42,400
Don't touch that.

630
00:38:42,400 --> 00:38:44,940
Is it possible there's unrepentance in?

631
00:38:44,940 --> 00:38:50,860
But then the last one, I would just like you to think, at the end of the day, this is what God wants for us.

632
00:38:50,860 --> 00:38:54,200
He wants us to be like a tree planted by streams of water.

633
00:39:01,340 --> 00:39:04,420
Do you know what happens to trees that are planted by streams of water when there's a drought?

634
00:39:04,420 --> 00:39:10,620
They're still thirsty, right?

635
00:39:10,620 --> 00:39:13,400
It's like, hey, I did the thing that I was supposed to do.

636
00:39:13,400 --> 00:39:16,340
I planted myself by a stream of water.

637
00:39:16,340 --> 00:39:17,820
I'm right by a source of water.

638
00:39:17,820 --> 00:39:19,480
Drought comes.

639
00:39:19,480 --> 00:39:20,640
They're still thirsty.

640
00:39:21,840 --> 00:39:23,240
Guess who's in charge of the drought?

641
00:39:23,240 --> 00:39:25,920
God is.

642
00:39:25,920 --> 00:39:30,200
So is it possible that you're doing the right stuff?

643
00:39:30,200 --> 00:39:33,220
You're like a tree planted by streams of water.

644
00:39:34,060 --> 00:39:41,180
And yet God is allowing the water levels to get lower and lower to invite you to deeper and deeper maturity.

645
00:39:41,180 --> 00:39:42,960
Guess what trees do when they experience drought?

646
00:39:42,960 --> 00:39:46,380
I learned some things this week.

647
00:39:46,380 --> 00:39:47,260
Are you guys proud of me?

648
00:39:48,560 --> 00:39:51,240
I don't know a whole lot about trees, but I learned some things this week.

649
00:39:51,240 --> 00:39:56,820
Trees, when they experience drought, they stop prioritizing shoot growth above the soil.

650
00:39:56,820 --> 00:40:02,520
And they divert that energy to create new tap roots below the soil to go deeper,

651
00:40:02,520 --> 00:40:05,400
to search for and find the water that is available to them.

652
00:40:06,360 --> 00:40:12,160
So, maybe you're like a tree planted by water, and God is allowing you to experience the season of drought.

653
00:40:12,160 --> 00:40:18,480
What if it's an invitation for you to stop prioritizing growth above the soil

654
00:40:18,480 --> 00:40:22,340
and start prioritizing root growth below the soil?

655
00:40:22,340 --> 00:40:27,440
Root systems, they're hard to study, right?

656
00:40:27,440 --> 00:40:31,300
Because they're not easy to observe.

657
00:40:31,300 --> 00:40:33,820
Science is about observing things.

658
00:40:34,900 --> 00:40:39,360
I think in the same way, Christians, we become so obsessed about what's happening above ground,

659
00:40:39,360 --> 00:40:44,460
we forget to be intentional to talk about what happens below the ground.

660
00:40:44,460 --> 00:40:45,920
This is what Jesus says.

661
00:40:45,920 --> 00:40:46,200
He says,

662
00:40:46,200 --> 00:40:50,880
Your Father who sees what is done in secret will reward you.

663
00:40:50,880 --> 00:40:54,400
As Christians, how often do we not talk about this stuff?

664
00:40:54,400 --> 00:40:59,300
We don't prioritize the things that happen when nobody's looking,

665
00:40:59,300 --> 00:41:01,300
because we don't get credit for that.

666
00:41:01,300 --> 00:41:03,720
Yes, we do.

667
00:41:03,920 --> 00:41:08,880
Your Father who sees what is done in secret will reward you.

668
00:41:12,380 --> 00:41:14,420
We get so fixated on the results.

669
00:41:14,420 --> 00:41:16,940
Go back to that Psalm 1 verse real quick.

670
00:41:16,940 --> 00:41:21,380
In season,

671
00:41:21,380 --> 00:41:24,740
it will yield its fruit.

672
00:41:24,740 --> 00:41:27,460
God is in charge of the fruit.

673
00:41:27,460 --> 00:41:30,780
He is in charge of the water level.

674
00:41:30,780 --> 00:41:32,000
All we can do

675
00:41:32,000 --> 00:41:34,040
is plant ourselves near Him

676
00:41:34,040 --> 00:41:35,580
and dig deeper into Him.

677
00:41:36,200 --> 00:41:36,800
It's been seasons for me.

678
00:41:36,800 --> 00:41:37,600
It's been seasons for me of drought

679
00:41:37,600 --> 00:41:41,840
that have caused me to prioritize new spiritual practices in my life.

680
00:41:41,840 --> 00:41:46,020
It's why we're committed to talking about spiritual practices over the next three years.

681
00:41:46,820 --> 00:41:48,880
So if you're in a season where God seems absent,

682
00:41:48,880 --> 00:41:51,280
I'd consider you to lean into some new spiritual practices,

683
00:41:51,280 --> 00:41:55,760
to move away from formula into mac and cheese.

684
00:41:56,380 --> 00:41:57,060
Right?

685
00:41:57,060 --> 00:41:59,440
Here's a couple that I think would help in this season.

686
00:41:59,440 --> 00:42:00,280
Number one, Sabbath.

687
00:42:00,280 --> 00:42:02,940
Take a day

688
00:42:02,940 --> 00:42:05,480
where you're not doing anything productive.

689
00:42:05,480 --> 00:42:08,480
You're just resting in God's presence.

690
00:42:09,780 --> 00:42:10,900
And you're okay.

691
00:42:10,900 --> 00:42:14,940
You're okay not accomplishing anything.

692
00:42:14,940 --> 00:42:17,800
Because it's not about what you bring to the table.

693
00:42:17,800 --> 00:42:19,200
It's about who brings you to the table.

694
00:42:19,200 --> 00:42:20,920
Take a rest.

695
00:42:20,920 --> 00:42:25,660
Silence and solitude.

696
00:42:25,660 --> 00:42:28,000
Can I be honest with you?

697
00:42:28,000 --> 00:42:30,160
I'm bad at this.

698
00:42:30,160 --> 00:42:34,360
I'm like 20 minutes into silence and solitude.

699
00:42:34,360 --> 00:42:36,480
I didn't hear from God yet.

700
00:42:36,480 --> 00:42:38,280
I'm like, all right, that didn't work.

701
00:42:38,280 --> 00:42:38,800
What's next?

702
00:42:40,780 --> 00:42:41,660
Man, just get away.

703
00:42:41,660 --> 00:42:42,280
Like, seriously.

704
00:42:42,280 --> 00:42:43,620
And here's the thing.

705
00:42:43,620 --> 00:42:44,840
In order to do this well,

706
00:42:44,840 --> 00:42:46,840
you're probably going to have to rely on your Christian community.

707
00:42:46,840 --> 00:42:49,760
That's why we love small groups here.

708
00:42:49,760 --> 00:42:51,820
Like, getting away for four hours,

709
00:42:51,820 --> 00:42:52,780
if you're a mom with kids,

710
00:42:52,780 --> 00:42:54,580
you're like,

711
00:42:54,580 --> 00:42:56,660
I feel like God's calling me to silence and solitude.

712
00:42:56,660 --> 00:42:57,500
How's that going to happen?

713
00:42:57,500 --> 00:43:00,380
Ask a friend.

714
00:43:00,380 --> 00:43:03,740
Let's do this together in community.

715
00:43:03,740 --> 00:43:09,500
Lectio Divino, another good option.

716
00:43:09,500 --> 00:43:10,480
We've talked about that a lot.

717
00:43:10,480 --> 00:43:11,960
Just pray.

718
00:43:11,960 --> 00:43:12,760
Seek God.

719
00:43:12,760 --> 00:43:16,120
See what he might want you to do to dig your roots down deeper.

720
00:43:16,120 --> 00:43:17,180
There's a promise in the Scriptures.

721
00:43:17,180 --> 00:43:19,040
Come close to God and God will come close to you.

722
00:43:19,040 --> 00:43:22,940
But sometimes we want that to happen on our timing and not his.

723
00:43:24,000 --> 00:43:25,340
So just keep drawing close.

724
00:43:25,340 --> 00:43:30,240
And just trust that his timing works.

725
00:43:31,820 --> 00:43:35,440
Okay, we're going to end singing a song.

726
00:43:35,540 --> 00:43:36,580
I asked Donovan to come up.

727
00:43:36,580 --> 00:43:40,500
It's a song called Heart of Worship.

728
00:43:40,500 --> 00:43:46,560
And this song was actually written out of a church who was in a season where life was pretty good.

729
00:43:47,620 --> 00:43:48,900
And yet God felt absent.

730
00:43:48,900 --> 00:43:50,000
It was a growing church.

731
00:43:50,000 --> 00:43:53,920
One of those big churches with lights and fog and a professional worship leader.

732
00:43:53,920 --> 00:43:54,580
You guys been there?

733
00:43:54,580 --> 00:43:57,060
It's pretty cool to worship at a church like that, right?

734
00:43:57,060 --> 00:43:58,160
You're like, this place is rocking.

735
00:43:58,160 --> 00:43:58,800
This is awesome.

736
00:43:58,800 --> 00:44:00,400
God must be in this place.

737
00:44:01,140 --> 00:44:09,360
And yet after a season, they realized, man, it feels like we're getting distracted by the stuff.

738
00:44:09,360 --> 00:44:11,800
We're missing God.

739
00:44:11,800 --> 00:44:14,000
So the pastor, I love this guy.

740
00:44:14,000 --> 00:44:15,460
I don't even know him, but he sounds awesome.

741
00:44:15,460 --> 00:44:17,400
He was like, hey, sound system, we're getting rid of it.

742
00:44:17,400 --> 00:44:18,520
Done.

743
00:44:18,520 --> 00:44:20,820
Lights, fog, gone.

744
00:44:20,820 --> 00:44:27,320
And their worship leader eventually wrote this song about this season, this heart of worship.

745
00:44:27,320 --> 00:44:28,920
We're getting rid of all of the other stuff.

746
00:44:30,220 --> 00:44:33,760
All of the distractions, all of the noise, and we're just coming back to the first love.

747
00:44:33,760 --> 00:44:35,580
The thing that matters most.

748
00:44:35,580 --> 00:44:39,320
So we're going to end by singing this.

749
00:44:39,320 --> 00:44:40,480
Let me read one more verse.

750
00:44:40,480 --> 00:44:42,100
Let's paraphrase.

751
00:44:42,100 --> 00:44:46,160
Eugene Peterson paraphrases Matthew 11 this way.

752
00:44:46,160 --> 00:44:47,020
He says, are you tired?

753
00:44:47,020 --> 00:44:48,700
Worn out?

754
00:44:48,700 --> 00:44:50,040
Burn out on religion?

755
00:44:50,040 --> 00:44:51,820
Come to me.

756
00:44:51,820 --> 00:44:54,420
Get away with me and you will recover your life.

757
00:44:54,420 --> 00:44:55,980
I'll show you how to take real rest.

758
00:44:55,980 --> 00:44:56,740
Walk with me.

759
00:44:56,740 --> 00:44:57,560
Work with me.

760
00:44:57,560 --> 00:44:59,160
Watch how I do it.

761
00:44:59,300 --> 00:45:00,740
Listen to this.

762
00:45:00,740 --> 00:45:03,460
Learn the unforced rhythms of grace.

763
00:45:03,460 --> 00:45:05,860
I won't lay anything heavy or ill-fitting on you.

764
00:45:05,860 --> 00:45:07,080
Keep company with me.

765
00:45:07,080 --> 00:45:09,200
Keep letting me into every room of your house.

766
00:45:09,200 --> 00:45:11,420
And you'll learn how to live freely.

767
00:45:11,420 --> 00:45:13,660
And lightly.

768
00:45:21,660 --> 00:45:38,040
Longing just to bring something that's worth that will blow.
